Package: vela-wallet
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Maintainer: Monday Labs <hello@getvela.app>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
# Security keys are opened directly (/dev/hidraw*), which needs a udev rule
# granting the logged-in user access. systemd 252+ ships one; `libu2f-udev` is
# the package for everything older. Recommends rather than Depends because the
# rule this package installs covers the same ground, and a modern systemd needs
# neither.
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers, libu2f-udev
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://getvela.app
Description: Self-custodial smart wallet for EVM networks
 Vela Wallet is a self-custodial smart account wallet for EVM networks.
 Accounts are Safe smart contracts with ERC-4337 account abstraction, and
 transactions are signed with a passkey - there is no seed phrase and no
 private key to store.
 .
 Balances and USD prices for 24 EVM networks appear in a single view, priced
 from on-chain DEX quotes with a Chainlink oracle fallback.
